---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy — PapaGaio">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 20 August 2026</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p style="max-width:640px;">
    PapaGaio has no ads and sells nothing to anyone. Everything stored is there
    to teach you a language or to see which pages get used.
  </p>

  <h2>Website</h2>
  <ul class="muted" style="max-width:640px; line-height:1.9;">
    <li>Your translation history is stored <strong style="color:var(--text)">only in your browser</strong> (localStorage). We never see it.</li>
    <li>Text you translate is sent to our server and forwarded to Groq (US) for processing. It is not stored on our side.</li>
    <li>A daily request counter per IP address exists purely to prevent abuse; it holds no content.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <ul class="muted" style="max-width:640px; line-height:1.9;">
    <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> runs always: page counts with no cookies and no cross-site tracking.</li>
    <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">Google Analytics</strong> loads <em>only</em> if you press Allow on the banner. Decline and the script is never fetched. Your choice is remembered in your browser; clear site data to be asked again.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Telegram bot</h2>
  <ul class="muted" style="max-width:640px; line-height:1.9;">
    <li>We store your Telegram user id, first name, learning progress and the cards you add. This is the product.</li>
    <li>Voice messages are transcribed by Groq (US) and are not kept after transcription.</li>
    <li>Dialog sessions with the AI coach keep only the recent turns needed for context, and are deleted at /stop.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Mobile app (Android and iPhone)</h2>
  <ul class="muted" style="max-width:640px; line-height:1.9;">
    <li>Tapping <strong style="color:var(--text)">Start here</strong> creates an anonymous account on our server. There is no email, no password and no social sign-in — the account is identified by a random token stored securely on your device.</li>
    <li>Tied to that token we keep your <strong style="color:var(--text)">learning progress</strong>: which cards you have answered, how you graded them and when each is due next. This is what lets the schedule survive a reinstall and stay in step with the Telegram bot if you pair them.</li>
    <li>Cards you write yourself are stored with the account, as is the text you send to the reader and the recent turns of a coach conversation.</li>
    <li>Voice recordings you make for pronunciation practice, and photos you point at Portuguese text, are sent for processing and are <strong style="color:var(--text)">not kept</strong> afterwards.</li>
    <li>The app has no advertising, no analytics SDK and no crash reporter. Nothing about you is sold or handed to advertisers.</li>
    <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">Delete everything from inside the app:</strong> Settings → Delete account. That erases the profile, the schedule, the review history, the cards you wrote and every paired device. It is immediate and cannot be undone.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <ul class="muted" style="max-width:640px; line-height:1.9;">
    <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">Cloudflare</strong> — hosting and database.</li>
    <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">Groq</strong> — translation, dialog, speech recognition and reading text from photos. Processing happens in the United States.</li>
    <li><strong style="color:var(--text)">Microsoft Edge TTS</strong> — audio synthesis (receives only the text to be spoken).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your data, your call</h2>
  <p class="muted" style="max-width:640px;">
    In the app: <strong style="color:var(--text)">Settings → Delete account</strong>,
    which removes everything at once. For the bot: send /pause and email
    <a href="mailto:agent@azenha.ai">agent@azenha.ai</a> — everything
    tied to your Telegram id will be deleted. Either way, write to us at the
    same address if you would rather we did it for you.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
